			"notes": "# Version 4.0.0\n\n## 📝Notes\nThis version made use of AI to help in development. The main issue with this mod was making versions for multiple minecraft modding frameworks (fabric, forge, neoforge), to solve this I've made use of [stonecutter](https://codeberg.org/stonecutter/stonecutter) which allows me to build for multiple versions off a single code base.\n\nAnother issue I've faced is testing these versions, it stacks up quite quickly since there are so many versions to build for. To solve this I've made use of [mineflayer](https://github.com/prismarinejs/mineflayer) which lets me create bots via scripting to go in to the server for automated testing.\n\nThese two other projects have made it really simple to build for this project, my next aim is to lower the jar file count by targetting versions which cover a wide range of minecraft versions instead of targetting them one by one. The code has always been simple, testing was the difficult part.\n\nSo far it looks to all be working with the changes showing passes in all automated and some manual tests, as always, please do let me know if any issues arise.\n\n## ✨ New\n  - Now supports **Fabric**, **NeoForge** and **Forge**, all built from one codebase.\n  - Supported versions:\n    - **Fabric:** 1.16.4 – 1.16.5, 1.18.2, 1.19 – 1.19.2, 1.20 – 1.20.1, 1.21 – 1.21.1, 1.21.11, 26.3 (needs Fabric API)\n    - **NeoForge:** 1.21 – 1.21.1, 1.21.11, 26.3\n    - **Forge:** 1.7.10, 1.12.2, 1.16.5, 1.18.2, 1.19.2, 1.20.1\n  - New config file that works the same on every loader: `config/sleepingserverstoppermod.properties`\n    - `shutdownTimeInMinutes=2` (minimum 1 minute)\n    - `shutdownOnLaunch=true`\n\n## 🐛 Fixes\n  - The shutdown now runs on the server thread.\n  - Joining and leaving over and over no longer stacks up shutdown timers.\n  - The countdown now starts on every version when the last player leaves. On 1.7.10 it never started.\n  - The countdown keeps working while a 1.21.2+ server is paused because it is empty.\n  - Players without the mod can now join 1.7.10 and 1.12.2 servers.\n  - The mod no longer does anything in singleplayer or on LAN worlds.\n\n## ⚠️ Upgrading from 3.x\n  - The old `sleepingserverstoppermod-common.toml` / `.cfg` config files are no longer read. Copy your values into the new `.properties` file, which is created on first launch."
		},
